It does the most damage and kills monsters fastest at +7--and the best
magical effects (curse absorption, 1-turn Elbereth, magic resistance)
are still equally potent.

At lower enchantments you'll get the lesser magical effects more
often.  Probing is nearly useless, especially if you have a
stethoscope.  Scaring isn't all that useful since if you want to do it
you can 1-turn E.  Stunning is even less useful than scaring.
Cancellation is completely useless except against a select few
monsters, but it's too unreliable to use against them.

If you think those 4 things are worth averaging a lot less damage,
that's up to you--personally I'd rather have the monsters attacking me
fewer turns.



